# EXAMPLE of the general D:\LLM configuration. Copy it as llm.conf (which is not
# committed) and adjust the values:
#   cp llm.conf.example llm.conf
#
# Read by Router/router.sh and the Git Bash aliases ("llama" command).
# Bash syntax: NAME="value", no spaces around "=".

# llama.cpp build used by the router: name of a folder in D:\LLM\Servers that
# contains llama-server.exe (e.g. llama-b11146-bin-win-vulkan-x64).
#   List builds and show the active one:  llama server
#   Switch build:                         llama server <folder>   (then llama stop + llama start)
#   Try another one without switching:    SERVER_BUILD=<folder> llama start
SERVER_BUILD="llama-bXXXXX-bin-win-vulkan-x64"
